  "id": "youssef-harby/weather-station-realtime-parquet",
  "title": "Weather Station Real-Time in Parquet",
  "description": "High-resolution environmental monitoring data collected by a Raspberry Pi with Enviro+ sensor and streamed directly to cloud storage in Parquet format. Each record captures timestamped atmospheric measurements including temperature, pressure, humidity, air quality gases (oxidised, reducing, NH3), light intensity, and particulate matter (PM1, PM2.5, PM10) across one or more named stations. The dataset is organized by station and date, enabling real-time and historical analysis of local atmospheric conditions.",
  "keywords": [
    "weather",
    "air-quality",
    "particulate-matter",
    "environmental-monitoring",
    "real-time",
    "climate-change"
